===============================================================================
Third-Party Software and External Geospatial Data Notice
===============================================================================

1. LeafMachine3 Computer Vision Engine (AGPL-3.0 Boundary)
   The automated installer (`setup_leafmachine3.sh`) clones LeafMachine3
   (Weaver 2026; https://github.com/Gene-Weaver/LeafMachine3) into an isolated
   local directory (`LeafMachine3/` with virtual environment `LeafMachine3/.venv`)
   and downloads its pretrained ONNX checkpoints into `models/lm3/`. This
   repository (`Packera_dubia_morphometrics`) neither bundles nor modifies
   LeafMachine3 source files, and Step 02 interacts with LeafMachine3 across a
   read-only configuration and ONNX Runtime boundary. LeafMachine3 itself is
   distributed separately by its authors under the GNU Affero General Public
   License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0).

2. Federal and Academic Geospatial Layers
   Environmental rasters and vector layers fetched at runtime into
   `data/environmental/` remain subject to the terms of their upstream
   providers:
   * U.S. Federal Public Domain (17 U.S.C. Section 105 / CC0 1.0): USDA-NRCS
     SSURGO Soil Data Access (SDA), USDA-NRCS SOLUS100 (doi:
     10.15482/USDA.ADC/25033856), USGS State Geologic Map Compilation (SGMC;
     doi: 10.5066/F7WH2N65), USGS 3D Elevation Program (3DEP) 1-arc-second DEM
     tiles, US EPA Level III Ecoregions, and USDA PLANTS county distributions.
   * Academic Research Datasets: POLARIS 30 m soil grids (Chaney et al. 2019;
     doi: 10.1029/2018WR022797) and WorldClim v2.1 bioclimatic rasters (Fick
     and Hijmans 2017; doi: 10.1002/joc.5086, distributed for academic and
     non-commercial research).
   * Digitized Herbarium Vouchers (GBIF and iDigBio): Specimen images and
     Darwin Core occurrence records downloaded into `data/raw_vouchers/` retain
     the copyright and Creative Commons license (`CC0`, `CC BY`, or `CC BY-NC`)
     assigned by each contributing herbarium (`institutionCode`).
